WEBVTT

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:02.460
This is the Flower
of Forgetfulness.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.130
I believe a Death Spirit
who recovers his memory

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.360
becomes a ghost because of
the attachment to his life on earth.

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:11.330
That's why, if his memory is erased
with this Flower of Forgetfulness...

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.030
But...

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:18.030
<i>- Staying a Death Spirit by losing</i>
- Whose fault do you think

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.460
<i>- by losing his memories</i>
- it is that I look like this?!

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:20.500
<i>- or becoming a ghost</i>
- You said it was the cat

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:21.530
<i>- by holding on</i>
- on the second block, right?

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.730
<i>- to the memories.</i>
- Y-Yeah, it's because of the cat.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.130
<i>- Which one would</i>
- The cat, the cat, the cat!

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.230
<i>- make Takuto happy?</i>
- Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.060
<i>I couldn't say it last night</i>
<i>or the night before.</i>

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:24.530
I'm going to say it tonight.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:25.830
Yeah.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:29.760
Hey, are you all made up,
graduate?

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.860
Takuto, you're coming too?

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:36.600
Stupid, do you think I would
miss your graduation?

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:38.030
Oh, right.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:41.400
Hey, hey,
if you're like that already,

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:44.230
you might even cry
before the graduation!

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:44.960
Huh?

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.400
Make sure to smile
as you graduate.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:48.760
Yeah!

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:05.930
<i>Wakana Kimura.</i>

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:06.860
Yes!

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.800
<i>Mitsuki Koyama.</i>

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:15.760
Yes!

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.360
Ma'am...

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:30.900
Congratulations.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:35.630
<i>Kumi Sagimiya.</i>

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:36.530
Yes!

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.730
Congratulations, Mitsuki.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.030
We finally graduated.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.560
It's farewell to
this school today.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:04.900
But next month, we're just moving
to the junior high next door.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:05.600
Yeah.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:10.560
I'm just so glad that I got to
graduate with all of you.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.060
Of course you'd
graduate with us!

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.160
Mitsuki.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.200
- We should be going soon.
- Oh...yes.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:21.800
Mitsuki!

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:24.100
Dr. Wakaoji...

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:44.860
This is the first time
I've come here with you.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:45.900
Yes.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:48.400
I am sorry.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:49.800
Grandma...

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:58.630
Dad, mom... I graduated from
elementary school today.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:07.400
Aoi, Hazuki, she will be thirteen
next month and go into junior high.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:12.560
I will take responsibility in
raising your daughter well.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:13.800
Grandma...

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:19.400
That's right. Mitsuki, there is still
a very long road ahead in life.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.030
Doctor Herberd,
who will be present at the surgery,

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:25.230
is set to arrive in
Japan next week.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.460
Thank you, Dr. Wakaoji.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:30.360
Sure.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.560
All right.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:42.060
Well, we do wanna end
with something great,

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.530
so maybe we could
do "Myself."

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.030
And then...

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:52.360
Do you want me to say it?

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.600
No, I'll say it.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:56.730
Say, Mitsuki.

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:59.460
Continuing our conversation
from before...

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.160
Huh?

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:02.630
The conversation about how
we should do the concert.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:03.730
Oh, yeah.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.730
I thought about the order of the songs,
but how about this?

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:07.800
Y-Yeah.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:09.400
Looks good.

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:12.800
Doesn't it? Now we have to
think about stage direction.

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:13.860
Mitsuki...

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:16.730
Actually, I won't do it today.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:21.800
We grew wings when
we did "Myself" before.

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:44.760
Is he okay?

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:45.760
Yeah.

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:46.730
But...

00:07:58.230 --> 00:07:59.230
Don't worry about it.

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:02.400
Leave your concert up to me.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.500
Of course I believe in you,
Takuto.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.200
But... But what if...

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:12.430
What if there is a way for you
to not have to become a ghost?

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:15.200
If there were a way,
I would have done it already.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:16.760
In that case...

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:18.600
Is there a way?

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:23.060
You become a ghost because
you recover your memory.

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:26.330
Isn't that true? Then...

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:29.030
You're saying I should
erase my memory again?

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:30.360
Y-Yes.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:33.100
No thanks.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:37.600
Just like how you graduated

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:40.130
from elementary school with
all sorts of memories,

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:43.360
I want to graduate from being
a Death Spirit with all my memories.

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:46.600
It's totally better
to do it that way

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:50.360
than to throw away all your memories
to be a Death Spirit forever.

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:51.660
Takuto...

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:55.000
I was able to make lots of
good memories this year.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.560
Most of all,
I was able to meet you.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:05.900
By being around you, I was able to
feel like I was making music too.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:08.730
It was fun.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:12.960
It's thanks to you that
I was able to sing.

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:17.300
I'm also really glad I...

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:45.230
Even I know that nothing is
going to happen by saying this.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:50.560
You are a human being
and I am a Death Spirit.

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:55.000
It's something no one
can do anything about, but...

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:11.500
I like you, Mitsuki.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:17.960
Well...I just wanted to say that.
But you can just forget about it.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:39.930
I guess it's one-sided.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:45.200
Oh man.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:19.930
Happy birthday, Mitsuki!

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:22.030
- Happy birthday!
- Happy birthday!

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:23.560
Thank you, everybody.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.360
You turned thirteen
before the rest of us!

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:28.800
You're so grown up!

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:33.060
Hey, hey, if a 13-year-old
is a grown-up, then what am I?

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:36.830
Oh, Ms. Oshige!

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.530
Hey, you seem too be
doing well.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:41.200
- Huh?
- Huh?

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:45.300
- Wow! Madoka Wakamatsu!
- Wow! Madoka Wakamatsu!

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:46.330
Hello!

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:47.400
Why?

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:52.200
To tell you the truth, I told her
that today was your birthday.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:55.860
And I came here
for my precious fan.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:59.530
Huh? Weren't you
a fan of Full Moon?

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:03.200
Huh? Well, I like Full Moon,
but I also like Madoka.

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:06.760
Well, that's fine.
Oh yeah, yeah.

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:10.600
I have a birthday present
for you in this backpack.

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:14.700
Wow, thank you very much.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.200
Open it and take a look.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:17.130
Okay.

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:18.700
This is...

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.360
It's a ticket for my concert
the day after tomorrow.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:23.760
By the way, Full Moon will
also be performing.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:25.030
It's the other way around!

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:27.560
You're performing in
Full Moon's concert.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.230
She never changes.

00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:32.200
I have ones for your friends too,
so all of you please come.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:35.560
Actually,
since we're fans of Full Moon...

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:38.460
- We already have tickets!
- We already have tickets!

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:39.200
What?!

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:42.830
Yeah, we all decided to go.

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:46.800
Then I'll give the tickets to
your Grandma and Ms. Tanaka.

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.730
I apologize, we also already...

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.200
It's my first show since
Fuyuko Komaki's dinner show.

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:55.230
Oh, what should I wear?

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:09.760
Now then, please give me your signature
on the surgery agreement.

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:12.360
Mitsuki, are you
all right with this?

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.830
Doctor, I will entrust
myself to you.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:17.660
Mitsuki, let's do our best.

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:18.800
Yes.

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:29.400
<i>I like you, Mitsuki.</i>

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:40.900
Eichi... What am I
supposed to do?

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:45.160
<i>Please forget about me.</i>
<i>You don't need to worry anymore.</i>

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:47.660
<i>You can just forget about it.</i>

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:51.100
<i>Why did both of them</i>
<i>say the same thing?</i>

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:57.700
<i>But this feeling...</i>

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:03.360
Why do I feel the same way
as when Eichi said it?

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:08.960
I don't wanna. I can't forget
about either Eichi or Takuto.

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:12.860
Because Takuto is...

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:27.700
One more day left.
At least tomorrow, I'll...

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:34.430
I see.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.400
I don't understand
these kinds of feelings.

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:40.430
How can I feel this way?

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:41.800
You can.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:46.560
It's okay to feel that way.
I was the same too.

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:52.560
When I was teamed up with Izumi,
I really liked him.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:03.930
At first, my feelings
didn't reach Izumi,

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:07.400
but after confessing my love to him
over and over again, finally...

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:16.330
But Izumi never really
opened his heart.

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.860
<i>Division Chief, why?!</i>

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:25.330
<i>Why do I have to pair up</i>
<i>with this newcomer? I'm...</i>

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:29.830
<i>Izumi Lio...has requested</i>
<i>to disband from you.</i>

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:37.760
<i>Izumi! Why did you...</i>

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:42.000
<i>A person's feelings are</i>
<i>unstable and unreliable.</i>

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:45.000
<i>That's why,</i>
<i>what you're saying...</i>

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:52.930
I thought that if I had to experience that,
I never wanted to be in love again.

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:58.900
However, when Takuto came around,
I started to like him.

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:03.460
Although in the end, my heart
was broken by Takuto as well.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:04.900
No way.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.930
It's okay.
I don't regret it at all.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:12.630
I'm fine if Takuto is happy.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:16.400
I bet Eichi feels the same way
about you too.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:17.560
Meroko...

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:23.130
Don't you like him? Why don't you be
more honest with your feelings?

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:25.730
But...

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:32.000
It doesn't mean
you'll forget Eichi at all.

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:35.730
You're alive. Of course
a new romance will begin.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:38.000
That's what it means to live.

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:45.530
What you have to do right now
is convey your true feeling.

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:51.600
Takuto will surely understand
if you tell him the truth.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:59.500
KOYAMA

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:01.300
Welcome home.

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:06.130
Izumi and Jonathan.

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:07.300
What do you want?

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.560
I was wondering
what happened.

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:13.130
Did you already have
Takuto drink it?

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:16.360
No, but I'm going to talk
to him about it now.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:18.200
Is that so?

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:21.030
Take care.

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:31.660
Izumi, you're not acting like yourself,
being so concerned about Mikki.

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:32.960
You think so?

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:38.360
Since some people
abandoned their work,

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:41.200
I wonder what's going to
happen to Mitsuki's fate.

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:45.460
Her fate probably
won't change though.

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:47.200
You think so?

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:52.300
Do you really think
that fate can't be changed?

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:02.800
What is that?

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:04.200
The Flower of Forgetfulness.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:08.600
It's the only way for you
to not become a ghost.

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:09.830
The Flower of Forgetfulness?

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:13.560
If you drink this,
you'll forget all your memories.

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:14.960
What do you mean all?!

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:17.560
Memories from when
you were a human,

00:18:17.600 --> 00:18:19.360
as well as after you
became a Death Spirit.

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:21.000
Y-You've got to be kidding.

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:24.400
But Takuto, if you don't drink it,
you'll become a ghost!

00:18:24.760 --> 00:18:26.130
Stupid, I already told you!

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:29.060
I'm gonna be around until
your concert is over!

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:34.500
But I don't want you to become
a ghost even after the concert is over!

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:36.360
Mitsuki...

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:38.160
Takuto, please.

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:41.530
No, I'm definitely not
going to drink it.

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:46.400
Why would you go that far to
try to make me drink this?

00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:54.130
Right now, I can touch
your hand like this.

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:57.960
But if you became a ghost...

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:04.300
I told you to forget
what I told you!

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.930
Wasn't that how you really feel?

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:12.100
I also want you to
always be by my side.

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:14.730
I don't want to lose you.

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:16.830
I...

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:21.230
If I can listen to your singing,
to Full Moon's singing, tomorrow,

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:22.530
then that's fine.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:25.100
Even if I become
a ghost after that.

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:28.760
I don't want that.
That's not fine at all!

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:32.360
Then it won't be Full Moon's
LIVE concert.

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:38.160
Doesn't live also mean "to live"?
That's what you taught me!

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:41.800
But then how can you be fine
with becoming a ghost?

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:47.500
This is your live concert. As long as
you have the passion to live...

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:48.760
You're wrong, Takuto.

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:52.230
Full Moon doesn't
just belong to me.

00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:58.130
I was wondering for a long time
what Full Moon is.

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:00.400
And I finally figured it out.

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:04.230
Full Moon is a dream that
Takuto and I created.

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:07.860
Meroko, Ms. Oshige, and Dr. Wakaoji...

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:10.530
Everybody helped to
build this dream.

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:16.900
You said it yourself. That you felt like
you were making music with me.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:23.500
Full Moon is a dream that can't be
seen without you and me together.

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:27.600
Full Moon's live concert
won't be a live concert

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:29.930
unless we feel that
we need to live.

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:31.200
Mitsuki...

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:35.600
Takuto...
Let's live together.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:40.200
Let's make tomorrow the first day
for the new you and me.

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:43.300
Yeah, you're right.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:48.900
Takuto... I like you.

00:23:06.800 --> 00:23:08.460
Mitsuki, I...

00:23:08.530 --> 00:23:13.500
Hey, Takuto, what are you doing here?
This is no time to be daydreaming.

00:23:13.930 --> 00:23:14.600
Meroko...

00:23:14.900 --> 00:23:17.130
There's no stopping now that
we've made it here.

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:20.200
We have to do
what we can do.

00:23:20.930 --> 00:23:23.460
Thanks, Meroko.
You're right.

00:23:24.060 --> 00:23:27.300
We have to prevent her from dying,
no matter what!

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:28.360
Yeah!

00:23:28.960 --> 00:23:32.060
Next time on Full Moon:
"The Fated Day."

00:23:32.600 --> 00:23:33.600
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
